Z||000000||DreXteR||10-14-2001||12:46 AM||||Well is not what you think. Is an easy mod to use a MOMO steering wheel w/o buy the expensive and controversial distance add of the adapter. Well is for 6  bolt pattern only. When you take off the Fiero Steering wheel, flip it and there is it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Now brake or take off the plastic cover from the Fiero steering wheel(facing the wheel in the normal position). Then take all 6 screws. Use a heavy pliers to push the screw area inward until reaching the disaire position. You will have to do this measuring time by time in the MOMO steering wheel holes patterns. When you finish move the 6 bolt supports, attach the MOMO wheel into the fiero hub.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>It works for me.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>This is my contribution to the so great and helpfull Forum.<P>DreX<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://users.centennialpr.net/drexter/Fiero/Fiero1.jpg">        <BR>  <BR>86 GT Turbo Intercooler Project - Total Restoration.<p>[This message has been edited by DreXteR (edited 10-14-2001).]||||reg||1
